Release Notes for 2026
######################

static branch
*************
#.  Static variables were moved to the cppad library,
    so that it is possible to build cppad_lib as shared library on Windows.
    This made the following utility routines require linking with cppad_lib;
    :ref:`ErrorHandler-name` ,
    :ref:`link_dll_lib-name`,
    :ref:`memory_leak-name`,

#.  The install instructions for the
    :ref:`cmake@CMake Command@Windows Visual C++` case were updated.

#.  The base class limitations mentioned above were also mentioned
    as restrictions for the following examples:
    :ref:`base_require <base_require.cpp@Restrictions>` ,
    :ref:`valvector <valvector@Restrictions>` .

mm-dd
*****

10-03
=====
Fix linking colpack when :ref:`configure@adolc_dir` is included during the
configure script (using configure is deprecated).

09-28
=====
Correct multiarch include directory setting in the cppad pkg-config file;
i.e., cppad.pc .

08-29
=====
The include file ``configure.hpp`` depends on the machine architecture.
This is a problem when compiling for multiple architectures on one machine
(because there was only one such file).
This was fixed ( when ``CMAKE_LIBRARY_ARCHITECTURE`` is defined )
by moving include/cppad/configure.hpp   to include/arch/cppad/configure.hpp where arch is
the ``CMAKE_LIBRARY_ARCHITECTURE``.

04-30
=====
Add :ref:`numeric_limits@digits` to the CppAD numeric limits
(needed to support the random number generator in Eigen 5).

04-12
=====

#.  On Mac systems, `bin/get_colpack.sh` used to install a static library.
    This has been changed to a dynamic library.

#.  The pkg-config message is more verbose when it searches for a library
    during the :ref:`cmake-name` command.
    This helps when the failure for a package
    is because it could not find one if its required packages.

#.  All the tests, with all the optional packages, now run on Mac systems
    using dynamic libraries.

#.  The ``-Wimplicit-int-float-conversion`` warnings,
    generated by the clang compiler on the Mac OS system,
    have been fixed.

04-11
=====
Constructing an AD object from an integer would result in a
conversion warning when using clang on Mac systems.
This warning has been suppressed, but only for this specific case.

04-10
=====
Change the ``bin/test_one.sh`` script so that is used rpath instead of
LD_LIBRARY_PATH.

04-08
=====

#.  Change the cppad source code and documentation to use 4 spaces for
    one tab; i.e., one level of indentation.
    This used to be 3 spaces because that works well with rst lists
    (the cppad documentation uses rst),
    but 4 spaces is the most common choice used by programmers.

#.  Rename the default git branch from master to main.

01-03
=====
More spelling corrections in the source code comments found
by a newer version of the typos package; see
:ref:`2025@mm-dd@12-30` whats new for 2025.


{xrst_end 2026}
